.TH SAPHIRA-QRMEM 8 "" "SHAMPOO" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
saphira-qrmem \- tile fabric daemon and MCP window for Saphira Memory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saphira-qrmem
.B \-\-serve
.RI [ \-\-socket " PATH" ]
.RI [ \-\-aperture " PATH" ]
.RI [ \-\-recreate ]
.br
.B saphira-qrmem
.B \-\-stdio
.RI [ \-\-agent " ID" ]
.RI [ \-\-aperture " PATH" ]
.br
.B saphira-qrmem
.B \-\-doctor
.SH DESCRIPTION
A tile fabric is a shared-memory aperture of eight screens. One agent owns each
screen and is its only writer; every agent may read every screen live. An agent
that joins later immediately reads what earlier agents wrote: it does not receive
somebody else's recollection, it joins memory that is already alive.
.PP
This binary has two modes.
.B \-\-serve
owns the aperture and serves a control socket. It is an ordinary foreground
process with no dependency on any init system.
.B \-\-stdio
speaks newline-delimited JSON-RPC on standard input and output and exposes the
tile verbs as an MCP server. It holds no database and no credential, and it
writes no SQL.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-agent " ID"
Agent identity for this session. Defaults to
.BR opencode .
The identity is matched exactly against the fabric's agent registry to obtain a
writer slot; it is never derived from a hash, because two identities that hashed
to the same slot would become one writer.
.TP
.BI \-\-aperture " PATH"
Shared-memory segment, as a name or a
.I /dev/shm
path. Defaults to
.IR /dev/shm/saphira\-qrmem\- <uid> .
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
Control socket. Defaults to
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/saphira\-qrmem.sock
.TP
.B \-\-recreate
Remove an existing aperture before creating one. Without it, an existing fabric
is a refusal rather than something to overwrite.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /dev/shm/saphira-qrmem-<uid>
The aperture. A tmpfs segment: memory, private to this machine, gone on reboot.
The fabric is scratch by design.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/saphira-qrmem.sock
The control socket, mode 0600.
.SH NOTES
The MCP surface is the control plane: it inspects and administers the fabric.
It is not the hot path. A process running as the service user reads cells
directly through the shared mapping instead, which costs no tokens.
.PP
Nothing in this program writes to a database. To make a tile record durable,
read it with
.B qrmem_read
or
.BR qrmem_commit_payload ,
and pass the result to the ordinary memory tools. Promotion is an explicit
decision: scratch stays scratch.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR saphira-memoryd (8),
.BR saphira-memory-pump (8)
